# 📚 Linked List (Part 4) - Doubly Linked List

## 📌 Introduction

A **Doubly Linked List (DLL)** is a type of Linked List where each node contains **three parts**:

- Previous Pointer (prev)
- Data
- Next Pointer (next)

Unlike a Singly Linked List, a Doubly Linked List allows traversal in **both forward and backward directions**, making insertion and deletion operations more flexible.

It is widely used in:

- Browser History
- Undo/Redo Functionality
- Music & Video Playlists
- LRU Cache
- Navigation Systems

