# 1️⃣ What is a Doubly Linked List?

## 📖 Definition

A Doubly Linked List is a linear data structure where each node stores:

- Previous Node Address
- Data
- Next Node Address

---

### Visualization

```
NULL ← [10] ⇄ [20] ⇄ [30] ⇄ [40] → NULL
```

Each node can move:

```
Forward →

Backward ←
```

---

# 2️⃣ Structure of a Node

### C++ Structure

```cpp
struct Node
{
    int data;
    Node* prev;
    Node* next;
};
```

---

### Memory Layout

```
---------------------------
| Prev | Data | Next |
---------------------------
```

---

# 3️⃣ Traversing a Doubly Linked List

Traversal can be performed in both directions.

---

### Forward Traversal

```
Head

↓

10 ⇄ 20 ⇄ 30 ⇄ 40
```

Output

```
10 20 30 40
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void display(Node* head)
{
    while(head != NULL)
    {
        cout << head->data << " ";
        head = head->next;
    }
}
```

---

### Backward Traversal

```
Tail

↓

40 ⇄ 30 ⇄ 20 ⇄ 10
```

Output

```
40 30 20 10
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

---

# 4️⃣ Insertion at Beginning

## 📖 Steps

Create new node

↓

Set next pointer to Head

↓

Update Head's previous pointer

↓

Move Head to new node

---

### Visualization

Before

```
20 ⇄ 30 ⇄ NULL
```

Insert

```
10
```

After

```
10 ⇄ 20 ⇄ 30
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(1)
```

