# 🔟 Singly vs Doubly Linked List

| Feature | Singly LL | Doubly LL |
|----------|-----------|-----------|
| Pointers | One | Two |
| Forward Traversal | ✅ | ✅ |
| Backward Traversal | ❌ | ✅ |
| Memory Usage | Less | More |
| Insertion/Deletion | Moderate | Easier |
| Implementation | Simple | Slightly Complex |

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Advantages

✅ Bidirectional traversal

✅ Easy deletion without searching previous node

✅ Better navigation

✅ Efficient implementation of LRU Cache

✅ Supports Undo/Redo operations

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Disadvantages

❌ Extra memory for previous pointer

❌ More pointer updates

❌ More complex implementation

---

