# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Doubly Linked Lists allow traversal in both directions.

✅ Every insertion/deletion requires updating **both previous and next pointers**.

✅ Always check for NULL before accessing pointers.

✅ Doubly Linked Lists are preferred when backward traversal is required.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Forgetting to update the previous pointer.

❌ Losing the Head or Tail pointer.

❌ Incorrect pointer order during insertion.

❌ Memory leaks after deletion.

---

# 📝 Summary

- A Doubly Linked List stores previous and next pointers.
- It supports forward and backward traversal.
- Insertion and deletion are more flexible than in Singly Linked Lists.
- It requires extra memory due to the additional pointer.
- Widely used in browser history, playlists, and LRU Cache implementations.

